  "problem": "${1}^{12}=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Here, ${1}^{12}$ is in exponent form. The base is $1$ and the exponent is $12.$ \n\nThis means that $1$ is taken as a factor $12$ times. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{1}^{12}={{1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1\\times 1}_{⏟}}_{12\\text{ times}}=1.\n$$",
